 division tic mostly  gathering gold caches and diptych chests  I was also taking down the odd boss -  but only if it was on my farming route  the only challenge was with the lack of  Ranger head of my weapons successful  dark zone farming is the best example of  being aware of what's going on around  you and being prepared as a solo player  with a poor build stealth is your friend  keep moving don't stop for anyone rogue  or otherwise if you find yourself in  trouble just run don't run wildly down  the middle of the street firing a gun  and every opportunity hug the buildings  always have something in front of you  and behind you run a concealed pulse and  trigger it off as often as possible keep  an eye on the kill feed it'll give you  all the information you need as far as  where the Rogues are on the map get  yourself familiar with your surroundings  plan a farming route and run it over and  over until you know every NPC every bit  of cover and all escape routes if you  need them  [Applause]  extractions  though a bit slower than the usual  speedruns are have without min/max  builds it's still perfectly achievable  with my trash tier skill power build  understanding the mission looking out  for the best cover and adjusting my  skills based on the NPC's but small  slip-ups were starting to come quite  unforgiving  [Music]  morning outsides invalid your position  you  these are actually a lot more difficult  mentioning they'd be I really had to set  camp utilizing any and all cover playing  very defensively I had to make sure I  was timing my skills I had a fresh flame  turret ready for the start of each wave  to slow down the rushes that would be  lane straight for me the other challenge  I all of the sudden had to be conscious  of was the timer  [Music]  are you talking is being  I'm not a huge fan at the underground I  think I burnt out on it a bit from  playing it too much when it was first  released in year 1 I didn't turn on any  of the modifiers it was just